---
title: Olive Garden Chicken Gnocchi Soup
description: Creamy copycat Olive Garden chicken and gnocchi soup with spinach and carrots.
source: https://tornadoughalli.com/olive-garden-chicken-gnocchi-soup/
author: Tornadough Alli
servings: 6
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
time required: 30 minutes
course: soup
cuisine: American
tags:
  - chicken
  - gnocchi
  - soup
  - olive garden
  - copycat
---

> Adapted from Tornadough Alli. Optional: add 1 cup chopped celery with the other vegetables. For a thicker soup, stir in 1 tbsp cornstarch mixed with 1 tbsp cold water.

In a #large Dutch oven{} or stock pot, melt @butter{4%tbsp} and @olive oil{1%tbsp} together.

Add @onion{1%small}(chopped), @carrots{1%cup}(shredded), and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). Cook until the onions are translucent.

Whisk in @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} and cook for ~{1%minute}. Slowly stir in @chicken broth{6%cups} and simmer until it starts to thicken.

Meanwhile, cook @mini potato gnocchi{16%oz}(1 package) according to package directions; drain and set aside. (You can also cook the gnocchi directly in the soup liquid.)

Add @milk{2%cups} and bring to a boil. Stir in @parsley flakes{2%tsp}, and season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Reduce heat and add the gnocchi, @fresh spinach{1%cup}(chopped), and @boneless skinless chicken breast{1%lb}(cooked and shredded). Simmer until heated through and thickened.
